llman had been Olympic champion in this event in 1904.  Bacon recaptured the Olympic record and set a new world of 55.0 in winning the final.  There was a delay in announcing the result, as Bacon had taken a wrong hurdle during the race.  He regained the proper course at the next hurdle, and the judges, after due consideration, decided that he had covered the correct distance.  In third place in the final was " [:a {:href "/athletes/69541"} "Jimmy Tremeer"] " (GBR), who had won the British 100 yard title in 1897."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78064"} "Charles Bacon"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "57.00 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "58.80 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "55.00 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78555"} "Harry Hillman"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "59.20 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "56.40 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "55.3est / at 2 yards (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69541"} "Jimmy Tremeer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "1:01.8 (1 h10)"] [:td {} "1:00.6 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "57.0est / at 15 yards (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:c